      },
      "note": "Items are {label, text}: label is the day ('Lun 17'), in a column w_em times the font size wide; text may take lines_by_count lines. Rows stack from the top with a gap between row_gap_em[1] and row_gap_em[0] times the size. All rows share one size: the largest from size_by_count down to floor x that size where everything fits; past that, a text that is still too long ends in an ellipsis. In drawtext, row i starts at start + i * stagger."
